european nations love their alliances  the franco-ottoman alliance the  anglo-portuguese alliance the triple  alliance and not to mention the swedish  anyone who isn't denmark alliance and  one alliance which often isn't discussed  probably because of the whole failure  thing was the league of the three  emperors which saw germany  austria-hungary and russia twice attempt  to ally together to maintain the balance  of power in europe this alliance was  obviously extremely powerful and given  its ability to change the face of the  continent why didn't it last why did the  league of the three emperors fail twice  so when it comes to alliances in the  late 19th century germany was fairly  promiscuous and the policy reason behind  this formulated by chancellor otto von  bismarck was fairly simple to hell with  france germany's creation had seen it  rip these lands from france in 1871 and  bismarck knew that one day france would  seek to get them back and that the best  way for him to prevent this was to  create a series of alliances that would  dissuade france from trying at all which  is why bismarck turned to his neighbours  to the east the vast russian empire led  by alexander ii  bismarck also looked to the south at the  austro-hungarian empire which was less  keen on the prussian leadership of  germany having recently lost a war to  them but nobody else liked it so tough  this alliance was agreed in 1873 and  it's important to note that this  alliance wasn't a formal one in the  sense of a declaration of war against  one meant one against all it was one in  which the three agree to not upset the  already existing balance of power to  help each other suppress revolts and to  provide some troops and equipment in  case of war involving a country not part  of the treaty sounds simple except that  a mere five years later the league of  the three emperors was over so why did  this happen well there were two reasons  the first was france after its previous  defeat france swiftly rearmed leading  bismarck to believe war was in sight as  such he publicly threatened a preemptive  invasion of france to stop this and the  russian emperor made it clear that if  this happened he'd invade from the east  the second reason was the balkans  specifically bulgaria in 1878 russia  decisively won a war against the ottoman  empire and as a result dictated its  allies bulgaria's expansion to this this  importantly gave russia access to these  ports in the aeg and made it a player in  the mediterranean everybody who was  already there freaked out and there were  rumblings of war as such germany offered  to mediate and settled on these borders  this upset the russians because they  lost their port and it also upset the  austro-hungarians who felt the russia  was inciting slavic rebellions and the  alliance probably broke up undeterred  bismarck pushed for a second much more  formal alliance which would condemn  france to having no friends in 1879 he  concluded the dual alliance with  austria-hungary in which both formerly  agreed to defend each other russia  wouldn't agree to a formal defensive  alliance and so instead bismarck  compromised the new alliance the league  of the three emperors would see russia  agree to discreetly support either  germany or austria in the event of a war  with an outside power and those two  agreed to support russia in a war  against britain for bismarck this was  enough and it eliminated the possibility  of germany having to fight a two-front  war and this time this alliance managed  to last for six years so what happened  the second time the balkans happened and  again it was bulgaria after the 1878  changes the bulgarian people living here  revolted against the ottoman empire and  they declared that they were joining the  rest of the semi-independent bulgaria  which promptly declared that it was now  independent whilst this was going on  serbia invaded lost but it had the  backing of austria-hungary who came to  their rescue russian leaders were  furious with their ally not consulting  them and so promptly dissolved the  alliance bismarck wanted to try again  but he was too busy being fired by the  new kaiser wilhelm ii as such russia  turned to france and the two signed an  alliance in 1894 which set the stage for  the alliance system leading to world war  one  i hope you enjoyed this episode and  thank you for watching with a special  thanks to my patrons james bissonette  kelly money maker mr wolf sky chappelle  corso wolff jerry lambda in adam stalter  jordan longley rodney martin wyan hockey  spencer lightfoot captain cydog marvin  cassell gustav swan buggily wiggly words  about books podcast robert wetzel  winston k wood aaron the white matthew  shipley alex schwinn maggie patzkowski  corey turner anthony beckett coppertone  the mukwopa spinning three plates  charles the first ben ivinson and  scottish trekkie
 

